| 7Z26-01605 | Add to Archive Dialog Box / How to call this dialog box / Parameters / Memory usage for Compressing | This means that 7-Zip is allowed to use up to "80%" of the total RAM size, for example, 26 GB usage that is 80% from 32 GB (RAM Size). | GUI_contract_unimplemented; original_GUI_behavior_not_exercised | [L143](C:/Users/evanh/Documents/Codex/2026-10-12/go/work/full-archive-baseline-20261012/manual/fm/plugins/7-zip/add.htm:143) |
| 7Z26-01606 | Add to Archive Dialog Box / How to call this dialog box / Parameters / Memory usage for Compressing | But the actual memory usage depends on other settings: "Compression method", "Dictionary size" and "Number of CPU threads". | GUI_contract_unimplemented; original_GUI_behavior_not_exercised | [L143](C:/Users/evanh/Documents/Codex/2026-10-12/go/work/full-archive-baseline-20261012/manual/fm/plugins/7-zip/add.htm:143) |
| 7Z26-01607 | Add to Archive Dialog Box / How to call this dialog box / Parameters / Memory usage for Compressing | Note: High memory usage, close to or greater than the total RAM size, can make the compression process several times slower than normal processing, since the system may use slow swapping of memory pages between RAM and storage. | GUI_contract_unimplemented; original_GUI_behavior_not_exercised | [L150](C:/Users/evanh/Documents/Codex/2026-10-12/go/work/full-archive-baseline-20261012/manual/fm/plugins/7-zip/add.htm:150) |
