| 7Z26-02458 | lzma-specification.txt / lzma file format | lc [0, 8] the number of "literal context" bits lp [0, 4] the number of "literal pos" bits pb [0, 4] the number of "pos" bits dictSize [0, 2^32 - 1] the dictionary size | SDK_ABI_not_exposed; conditional_SDK_requirement_not_a_GUI_requirement | [L43](C:/Users/evanh/Documents/Codex/2026-10-12/go/work/full-archive-baseline-20261012/sdk-source/DOC/lzma-specification.txt:43) |
| 7Z26-02459 | lzma-specification.txt / lzma file format | The following code encodes LZMA properties: | SDK_ABI_not_exposed; conditional_SDK_requirement_not_a_GUI_requirement | [L48](C:/Users/evanh/Documents/Codex/2026-10-12/go/work/full-archive-baseline-20261012/sdk-source/DOC/lzma-specification.txt:48) |
| 7Z26-02460 | lzma-specification.txt / lzma file format | void EncodeProperties(Byte *properties) { properties[0] = (Byte)((pb * 5 + lp) * 9 + lc); Set_UInt32_LittleEndian(properties + 1, dictSize); } | SDK_ABI_not_exposed; conditional_SDK_requirement_not_a_GUI_requirement | [L50](C:/Users/evanh/Documents/Codex/2026-10-12/go/work/full-archive-baseline-20261012/sdk-source/DOC/lzma-specification.txt:50) |
| 7Z26-02461 | lzma-specification.txt / lzma file format | If the value of dictionary size in properties is smaller than (1 << 12), the LZMA decoder must set the dictionary size variable to (1 << 12). | SDK_ABI_not_exposed; conditional_SDK_requirement_not_a_GUI_requirement | [L56](C:/Users/evanh/Documents/Codex/2026-10-12/go/work/full-archive-baseline-20261012/sdk-source/DOC/lzma-specification.txt:56) |
| 7Z26-02462 | lzma-specification.txt / lzma file format | #define LZMA_DIC_MIN (1 << 12) | SDK_ABI_not_exposed; conditional_SDK_requirement_not_a_GUI_requirement | [L59](C:/Users/evanh/Documents/Codex/2026-10-12/go/work/full-archive-baseline-20261012/sdk-source/DOC/lzma-specification.txt:59) |
