    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.8746bcf6ca5a60cf107a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Links are shown in Explore visualizations for the results from the correlation’s source data source. A link is assigned to one of the fields from the result provided in the correlation configuration (the results field). Each visualization displays fields with links in a different way ([Correlations in Logs Panel](../use-correlations-in-visualizations/#correlations-in-logs-panel) and see [Correlations in Table](../use-correlations-in-visualizations/#correlations-in-table)).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Correlation",
        "Source data source and result field"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/administration/correlations/correlation-configuration/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f01ef51d6708806dc074f63e55f543c0408d633b",
        "sha256": "fb4525128741c7b02cd6822866bed335a5a601af49f7ae89cdb7775390d7a0e1",
        "lineStart": 36,
        "lineEnd": 38,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/administration/correlations/correlation-configuration/index.md#L36-L38"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.a74aabcc92898bedd759",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "The target query is run when a link is clicked in the visualization. You can use the query editor of the selected target data source to specify the target query. Source data results can be accessed inside the target query with variables.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Correlation",
        "Target query"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/administration/correlations/correlation-configuration/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "f01ef51d6708806dc074f63e55f543c0408d633b",
        "sha256": "fb4525128741c7b02cd6822866bed335a5a601af49f7ae89cdb7775390d7a0e1",
        "lineStart": 42,
        "lineEnd": 42,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/administration/correlations/correlation-configuration/index.md#L42-L42"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.e0533d2b8147dd49443a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can use variables inside the target query to access the source data related to the query. Correlations use [Grafana variable syntax](../../../dashboards/variables/variable-syntax/). Variables are filled with values from the source results when the link is clicked. There are two types of variables you can use:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Correlation",
        "Target query",
        "Correlation Variables"
      ],
      "source": {
