    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.5305d1bede98916d8365",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To give grizzly access to your Grafana OSS/Enterprise instance and the Grafana Cloud Instance, you need to create a [service account](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana-cloud/account-management/authentication-and-permissions/service-accounts/) and a corresponding [access token](https://www.grafana.com/docs/grafana-cloud/account-management/authentication-and-permissions/service-accounts/#service-account-tokens) on each instance. You can use these tokens to authenticate requests to pull and push resources. Follow these steps on your Grafana OSS/Enterprise instance:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Migrate from Grafana OSS/Enterprise to Grafana Cloud manually",
        "Migrate Grafana resources",
        "Migrate dashboards, folders, data sources, library panels, and alert rules using Grizzly"
      ],
