      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "unresolved-no-explicit-oss-products-label",
        "products": []
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.2e5d025f11daf8b77172",
      "syntaxRole": "procedural-step",
      "sourceText": "1. To export your Reports, you will need to invoke the `api/reports` endpoint of your Grafana OSS/Enterprise instance. The below shell command accomplishes this by using `curl` to send a request to the endpoint and then stores the retrieved report configuration into a file named `reports.json`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Migrate from Grafana OSS/Enterprise to Grafana Cloud manually",
        "Migrate Grafana resources",
        "Migrate reports and playlists using Grafana’s HTTP API",
        "Reports (For Grafana Enterprise only)"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/administration/migration-guide/manually-migrate-to-grafana-cloud.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "ec67ca7782261b3d96c30c162036cf6fe27e88b5",
        "sha256": "c9d95a24ed04bfff932d37d3bc549d6e090c208de06681aefa008a7d06eef4b7",
