    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.318991abbc97fbbcaca6",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can add HTTP headers to all requests sent to data sources managed by Grafana provisioning Configure the header name in the `jsonData` field and the header value in `secureJsonData`. The following example sets the `HeaderName` header to have the value `HeaderValue` and the `Authorization` header to have the value `Bearer XXXXXXXXX`:",
      "headingPath": [
        "Provision Grafana",
        "Data sources",
        "Example data source configuration file",
        "Custom HTTP headers for data sources"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/administration/provisioning/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "a6caad47dea63fb1a213a61490f8f587ad16bba2",
