    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.0d63e2e0233b70aa4bf4",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "RBAC can be used to manage access to [app plugins](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/administration/plugin-management/#app-plugins). Each app plugin grants the basic Viewer, Editor and Admin organization roles a default set of plugin permissions. You can use RBAC to restrict which app plugins a basic organization role has access to. Some app plugins have fine-grained RBAC support, which allows you to grant additional access to these app plugins to teams and users regardless of their basic organization roles.",
      "headingPath": [
        "RBAC for app plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/rbac-for-app-plugins/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e4186760f49dbcfa912c522d97c34671a2ac1093",
        "sha256": "616dd8e22f0a5ec06391c91af75f471c1d2f3c352b2c88e42c9505689b0ec89f",
        "lineStart": 41,
        "lineEnd": 44,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/rbac-for-app-plugins/index.md#L41-L44"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f979f3e478c30c14ab5d",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "By default, Viewers, Editors and Admins have access to all App Plugins that their organization role allows them to access. To change this default behavior and prevent a basic organization role from accessing an App plugin, you must [update the basic role's permissions](ref:manage-rbac-roles-update-basic-role-permissions). See an example of [preventing Viewers from accessing an app plugin](ref:restrict-access-to-app-plugin-example) to learn more. To grant access to a limited set of app plugins, you will need plugin IDs. You can find them in `plugin.json` files or in the URL when you open the app plugin in the Grafana Cloud UI.",
      "headingPath": [
        "RBAC for app plugins",
        "Restricting access to app plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/rbac-for-app-plugins/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e4186760f49dbcfa912c522d97c34671a2ac1093",
        "sha256": "616dd8e22f0a5ec06391c91af75f471c1d2f3c352b2c88e42c9505689b0ec89f",
        "lineStart": 48,
        "lineEnd": 51,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/rbac-for-app-plugins/index.md#L48-L51"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.fb33e399b28c125fc214",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Note that unless an app plugin has fine-grained RBAC support, it is not possible to grant access to this app plugin for a user whose organization role does not have access to that app plugin.",
      "headingPath": [
        "RBAC for app plugins",
        "Restricting access to app plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/rbac-for-app-plugins/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e4186760f49dbcfa912c522d97c34671a2ac1093",
        "sha256": "616dd8e22f0a5ec06391c91af75f471c1d2f3c352b2c88e42c9505689b0ec89f",
        "lineStart": 53,
        "lineEnd": 53,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/rbac-for-app-plugins/index.md#L53-L53"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4a19f91529ea653bf22b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Plugins with fine-grained RBAC support allow you to manage access to plugin features at a more granular level. For instance, you can grant admin access to an app plugin to a user with Viewer organization role. Or restrict the Editor organization role from being able to edit plugin resources.",
      "headingPath": [
        "RBAC for app plugins",
        "Fine-grained access to app plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/rbac-for-app-plugins/index.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "e4186760f49dbcfa912c522d97c34671a2ac1093",
        "sha256": "616dd8e22f0a5ec06391c91af75f471c1d2f3c352b2c88e42c9505689b0ec89f",
        "lineStart": 57,
        "lineEnd": 58,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/rbac-for-app-plugins/index.md#L57-L58"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "excluded-by-explicit-document-products",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.7d675f614121445318e7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For a centralized reference of all Grafana Cloud app plugin roles, default permissions by basic role, and available plugin roles, refer to [Grafana Cloud app plugin role definitions](ref:plugin-role-definitions). Some plugins also have dedicated RBAC documentation with additional context and use cases, linked in the table below.",
      "headingPath": [
        "RBAC for app plugins",
        "Fine-grained access to app plugins"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/administration/roles-and-permissions/access-control/rbac-for-app-plugins/index.md",
