    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9cf8cb37420dfe9c1943",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "You can pause alert rule evaluation to prevent noisy alerting while tuning your alerts. Pausing stops alert rule evaluation and doesn't create any alert instances. This is different to [mute timings](ref:mute-timings), which stop notifications from being delivered, but still allows for alert rule evaluation and the creation of alert instances.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure Grafana-managed alert rules",
        "Configure alert evaluation behavior"
