    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f939503b8ddfa92cc6c7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For users working with Grafana's legacy alerting system, templates can still be utilized to extract useful information from alert conditions. However, it's important to note that you cannot use `$labels` to print labels from the query if you are using classic conditions, and must use `$values` instead. The reason for this is classic conditions discard these labels to enforce uni-dimensional behavior (at most one alert per alert rule). If classic conditions didn't discard these labels, then queries that returned many time series would cause alerts to flap between firing and resolved constantly as the labels would change every time the alert rule was evaluated.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Labels and annotations template examples",
        "Legacy Alerting templates"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/alerting-rules/templates/examples.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c718129b7843bc0a207cf7bfedf9661f59492299",
        "sha256": "91902c0ea7751e66d0d61d07304ff5e6a5317f5e1017166620afc6dce25e5af1",
        "lineStart": 260,
        "lineEnd": 260,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/alerting-rules/templates/examples.md#L260-L260"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.367eeeb6c0395a300e00",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Instead, the `$values` variable contains the reduced values of all time series for all conditions that are firing. For example, if you have an alert rule with a query A that returns two time series, and a classic condition B with two conditions, then `$values` would contain `B0`, `B1`, `B2` and `B3`. If the classic condition B had just one condition, then `$values` would contain just `B0` and `B1`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Labels and annotations template examples",
        "Legacy Alerting templates"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/alerting-rules/templates/examples.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "c718129b7843bc0a207cf7bfedf9661f59492299",
        "sha256": "91902c0ea7751e66d0d61d07304ff5e6a5317f5e1017166620afc6dce25e5af1",
        "lineStart": 262,
        "lineEnd": 262,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/alerting-rules/templates/examples.md#L262-L262"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.f2cde25c07ca39b5e7e7",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "To print all labels of all firing time series use the following template (make sure to replace `B` in the regular expression with the Ref ID of the classic condition if it's different):",
      "headingPath": [
        "Labels and annotations template examples",
        "Legacy Alerting templates",
        "Print all labels from a classic condition"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/alerting-rules/templates/examples.md",
