    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.ec6a37572164c3e8092a",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Rule-specific silences are silences that apply only to a specific alert rule. They're created when you silence an alert rule directly using the **Silence notifications** action in the UI.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure silences",
        "Rule-specific silences"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/configure-notifications/create-silence.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "de5f69c5f966165e5d158e3ae6eb7d57492999df",
        "sha256": "ff597f9ab4f6d6c3ee468bb3541225d07e825bdc5fede70457447577b64db7c0",
        "lineStart": 197,
        "lineEnd": 197,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/configure-notifications/create-silence.md#L197-L197"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.dcbd1648a0ba38ab9c4b",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "As opposed to general silences, rule-specific silence access is tied directly to the alert rule they act on. They can be created manually by including the specific label matcher: `__alert_rule_uid__=<alert rule UID>`.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure silences",
        "Rule-specific silences"
      ],
      "source": {
