    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.33c10f4e236482f89b50",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Inhibition rules suppress notifications for target alerts when a related source alert is already firing. For more information, refer to [Configure inhibition rules](ref:configure-inhibition-rules).",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure silences",
        "Inhibition rules"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/configure-notifications/create-silence.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "de5f69c5f966165e5d158e3ae6eb7d57492999df",
        "sha256": "ff597f9ab4f6d6c3ee468bb3541225d07e825bdc5fede70457447577b64db7c0",
        "lineStart": 221,
        "lineEnd": 221,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/configure-notifications/create-silence.md#L221-L221"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.6f7a23c13a398ed51c21",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "An inhibition rule suppresses notifications for target alerts when source alerts with matching label values are already firing. This lets you reduce noise when a root-cause alert makes dependent alerts redundant.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure inhibition rules"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/configure-notifications/inhibition-rules.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3030f57a20ca73738b38302be6ed815ab5155afb",
        "sha256": "756dc8fef9a59086b0fc06a046eba9ded48a3a12e3e252479ddbb3dd21e47dc5",
        "lineStart": 47,
        "lineEnd": 47,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/configure-notifications/inhibition-rules.md#L47-L47"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.4aff3f63f55f6cfd3aa3",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "For example, if a node is down (the **source**), you can inhibit all alerts for services running on that node (the **target**). This prevents your team from receiving individual alerts for each affected service when the underlying cause is already captured in the source alert.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure inhibition rules"
      ],
      "source": {
        "path": "docs/sources/alerting/configure-notifications/inhibition-rules.md",
        "gitBlobSha": "3030f57a20ca73738b38302be6ed815ab5155afb",
        "sha256": "756dc8fef9a59086b0fc06a046eba9ded48a3a12e3e252479ddbb3dd21e47dc5",
        "lineStart": 49,
        "lineEnd": 49,
        "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grafana/grafana/6193dc03311b631b9727b560d24369e683dc396e/docs/sources/alerting/configure-notifications/inhibition-rules.md#L49-L49"
      },
      "applicability": {
        "status": "oss-labelled-source-candidate-not-yet-reviewed",
        "products": [
          "cloud",
          "enterprise",
          "oss"
        ]
      },
      "atomicity": "unreviewed-may-require-splitting-or-deduplication",
      "acceptanceContract": null,
      "verificationStatus": "not-tested"
    },
    {
      "id": "grafana.candidate.9abbbba859322d7c25c6",
      "syntaxRole": "declarative-or-imperative-paragraph",
      "sourceText": "Inhibition rules are assigned to a [specific Alertmanager](ref:alertmanager-architecture) and only suppress notifications for alerts managed by that Alertmanager.",
      "headingPath": [
        "Configure inhibition rules"
      ],
      "source": {
